    <string name="key_help_instagram">On instagram.com, open Create (+) → Live video and copy the “Stream key”. Instagram gives a new key for every broadcast.</string>
    <string name="key_help_tiktok">In TikTok LIVE Center, open the stream key screen and copy the Server URL and the Stream key. Your account needs RTMP access; TikTok gives a new key for every broadcast.</string>
    <string name="key_help_youtube">In YouTube Studio, open Create → Go live → Streaming software and copy the “Stream key”. The key stays the same until you reset it.</string>
    <string name="key_help_facebook">On facebook.com, open Live video → Streaming software and copy the “Stream key”. Unless you turned on a persistent key, Facebook gives a new one for every broadcast.</string>
    <string name="key_help_twitch">In the Twitch Creator Dashboard, open Settings → Stream and copy your primary stream key.</string>
    <string name="key_help_kick">On Kick, open Creator Dashboard → Settings → Stream URL &amp; Key and copy the key. If it shows a different Stream URL, replace the server address with it.</string>
    <string name="key_help_custom">Paste the RTMP or RTMPS address and the stream key your server gives you.</string>
    <string name="server_placeholder">rtmp://your.server/live</string>
    <string name="live_reminder_instagram">Now press “Go live” in Instagram; the stream becomes public only after that.</string>
    <string name="live_reminder_tiktok">Check TikTok LIVE Center; you may need to start the stream there too.</string>
    <string name="live_reminder_youtube">If auto-start is off, press “Go live” in YouTube Studio.</string>
    <string name="live_reminder_facebook">Facebook shows a preview first; press “Go live” there to make it public.</string>

